{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-80133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the value of $ϕ?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-80133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+10\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =5 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-80133" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "acc111648e98b3a7ad24643b1110f946f793c19d0f12e1979e915333edd2152a"} {"question" "q-80133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-80133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(10)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{5})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{5}{2})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-80133" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(5)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-80147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)≈$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-80147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{4}{2\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\sqrt{2} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\sqrt{2}) \\\\  & =0.955\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}+{4}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡ϕ+{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =8+16 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =24 \\\\ R & =2\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.955)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-80147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "acc111648e98b3a7ad24643b1110f946f793c19d0f12e1979e915333edd2152a"} {"question" "q-80147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-80147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-1.156)"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.916)"] ["math" "2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.955)"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-1.054)"] ["math" "\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.854)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-80147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x-0.955)"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $R>0,$ what is the value of $R?$\n\n$R=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for cosine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+5\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2 \\\\ R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSquaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & =(2)^{2}+(5)^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+25 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =29 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "acc111648e98b3a7ad24643b1110f946f793c19d0f12e1979e915333edd2152a"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-274608" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{29}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-327723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that the expression $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)$ can be written as $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+ϕ)$ with ${0}^{∘}<ϕ<{90}^{∘}$ and $R>0$, what is the **exact** value of $ϕ?$\n\n$ϕ=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡($ \n{{field-1}} $)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-327723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The sum formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude-phase form\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x+ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{5}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-327723" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "acc111648e98b3a7ad24643b1110f946f793c19d0f12e1979e915333edd2152a"} {"question" "q-327723" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-327723" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{5}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-327982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ in the form $R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ)$ with $ϕ\\in (0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$ Use the **exact value** for $R,$ and round $ϕ$ to **three decimal places**.\n\n$5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x≈$\n{{field-1}}\n$\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x\\,-$\n{{field-2}}$)$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-327982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The difference formula for sine gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ) & =R(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ) \\\\  & =R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, by writing the given expression in the amplitude–phase form\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=R\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x) & =(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating coefficients, we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=5 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ ϕ & =arctan\\,(\\frac{2}{5}) \\\\ ϕ & ≈0.381\\,\\text{rad},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.\n\nFor the amplitude,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{R}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{R}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ & ={2}^{2}+{5}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =4+25 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =29 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x)≈\\sqrt{29}sin\\,(x-0.381).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-327982" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "acc111648e98b3a7ad24643b1110f946f793c19d0f12e1979e915333edd2152a"} {"question" "q-327982" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-327982" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{29}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-327982" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"} {"question" "q-327982" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.381"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981361/state.json" "file_sha256" "362606b2d3c7c0c483cf702354653a00175ee4ae28a319b33b88a90a13792ce2"}] "usage" {} "basis" 886 "retractions" [] "immutable_answers" [] "immutable_fields" [] "no_history" []}
